"Aline Dyce has enrolled three students in five years who had no card, on Hallick's word."
"Dyce keeps a second ledger, hidden in the record room, of work the Institute does unpaid."
"The Institute's licence to teach is granted by the Academy, and lapses if it is ever reviewed."
"Hallick's chamber holds a bed, a stove and a wall of books he brought from Geldor."
"Hallick sleeps at the Institute more nights than at his house on Hill Road."
"The record room's oldest boxes hold sequences the Institute has taught since before the Academy."
